      <Comment>Quercetin is a plant flavonol that is found in many fruits, vegetables, leaves, seeds, and grains. It was first isolated from an oak tree (genus |FRAME: TAX-3511|) hence its name. Quercetin has a bitter flavor and is used as an ingredient in dietary supplements, beverages, and foods. It is one of the most abundant dietary flavonoids. The compound was shown to act as a competitive inhibitor of |FRAME: EC-4.2.1.59| (FabZ) from the pathogenic bacterium |FRAME: TAX-210| |CITS: [18780820]|.</Comment>
